WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
Moments ago, Vice

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.601
President Kamala

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.570
Harris arrived in Nashville,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.604
where she is

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.539
meeting with state legislators and gun

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.340
reform advocates

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.608
amid the fallout from Tennessee

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.877
state Republicans decision to expel

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.846
two elected Democrats, Justin J.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.214
Pearson and Justin Jones

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:15.081
from the legislature.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:15.749
Jones

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.083
and Pierson broke House

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.752
decorum rules to participate

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.319
in gun reform

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.720
protests on the

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.756
legislative floor in response

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:24.457
to the deadly Nashville school shooting.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.026
This is only the third time

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.093
that state lawmakers

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.028
have been expelled

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.629
from the Tennessee legislature

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.231
since the Civil War.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:31.531
With us

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.832
now, Republican Tennessee state

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.368
lawmaker Brian Ritchie.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.302
Representative Ritchie,

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.070
thanks for joining us, sir.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.972
You were one of seven Republicans

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.107
who voted against expelling Democrat

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.409
Gloria Johnson

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:43.843
and one of just three Republicans

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.478
who voted against expelling

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.714
Representative Justin Pierson.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.116
But you did vote to expel Representative

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.351
Justin Jones.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.153
Can you explain your votes to us?

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.588
Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.289
So

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.358
I started sharing with leadership

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:58.892
and everybody

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.959
that I did not think

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.361
that expulsion was the right thing.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.696
What these three individuals did was

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:05.565
completely horrible.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.033
It was a disrespect

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.435
to our General Assembly.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.603
Those members that have served before me

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.872
and that will serve in the future.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.174
According to Article two, Section

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.408
12 of our Constitution.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.277
Did it constitute them being expelled?

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.511
Absolutely.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.713
In my opinion, was it warranted?

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.849
And I did not believe so.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.684
Representative Jones, his office is right

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:25.652
next door to mine.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.153
I had multiple conversations with him

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:27.654
this week.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.622
Let him know that I wasn't in favor.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:33.059
And essentially he told me that he wanted

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:33.827
to be kicked out

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:36.062
because his following was grow.

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:36.496
And he's

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.631
getting all this national exposure

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:41.067
and that the Metro City Council

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.602
had already

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:45.105
said that they were going to reappointing

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.473
back to the General Assembly.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.074
So I was honoring his wishes

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.576
and voting for him,

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.710
but I didn't think that any of them

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.412
should end up getting kicked out,

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.547
even though it was warranted

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.349
based on the letter of the law.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.818
So Republicans voted to expel

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.253
two young black men

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.055
and not the 60 year old white

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.923
woman, Representative Gloria Johnson,

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.892
who did the same thing.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:09.095
Johnson says that that's because she's

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:09.729
white.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.066
What do you think of that and

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.301
how do you think this looks

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.670
to the rest of the country?

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:20.140
And that's political nonsense.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.909
If anything, it was too energetic,

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.577
youthful males

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.213
that were a little bit more animated

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.082
while they were up there. And MS.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.283
Gloria Johnson, representing

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.851
Johnson, stood their seat

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.686
when the they played the video.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.321
It clearly showed her

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.956
standing there, not doing as much.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:39.092
And I think that swayed other members

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.793
to not vote for her.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.662
And that's why she's still there.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.663
Had nothing to do

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:44.864
with the color of their skin.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.633
I respect all three of them

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.001
and their constituents

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:48.835
that voted for them.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.837
I felt that they should stay.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.372
I honored Representative Jones,

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.740
but I had nothing to do with race.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:54.707
Anybody that statement

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.510
that was just trying to talk up

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.678
political nonsense,

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.813
that should not be discussed.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.017
So I guess one of the other reasons

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:05.518
that this has

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:05.985
gotten so much

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.320
attention is just because

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:07.921
the punishment

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.822
seems so much harsher than the

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.692
than the offense.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.028
And as you know, last year

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:16.095
the former state House

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:16.930
speaker, Republican

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.231
Representative Glenn Casado,

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.432
he was indicted

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:22.368
and arrested on federal bribery charges.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:23.803
He's contesting that.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.372
But he wasn't expelled for that in 2018

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:27.874
Republican state lawmaker

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:28.675
David Byrd

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.243
as we covered on our show at the time,

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.678
he was accused of sexually assaulting

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:32.212
three teenage

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.413
girls years

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.714
before when they were on his high school

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.182
basketball team.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.685
He was not expelled.

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.620
If Republicans are so concerned

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.889
about decorum and conduct

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:45.491
why would burn and Byrd and Casada

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:46.092
be allowed

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:48.027
to keep their seats

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.896
as long as they wanted.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.198
While these two gentlemen were ejected

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.199
and expelled,

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:56.903
I, I was not.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.238
I'm a freshman lawmaker.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:03:59.272
I just got elected.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.841
I can't speak of what happened last year.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.710
20. 18.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.111
I know that the conversation

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.112
that was taking place

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:06.813
among the

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.082
Republican Party this week is

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.083
this is the first time

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.217
that this has happened

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.785
in any of our lifetime.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.421
As far as for somebody just blatantly

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.691
coming out and

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.728
disrupting our floor session

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.630
and that a precedent had to be set.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:23.963
And that's

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.999
what the Republican Party was sharing

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.033
as they were going around

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.235
and chatting among each other.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.671
But not once did it end up coming up.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.172
As far as

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.508
anything that happened in the past.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.043
It was based on this right here.

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.578
And this had not happened

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.779
in any of our lifetime.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.080
And we needed to set a precedent.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.081
I didn't agree with it.

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.517
That's why I was against the expulsion.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.986
But according to Article two, Section 12,

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.721
it's there in black and white

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.622
So, I mean, I guess

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:51.658
the issue

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:52.659
another reason that

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:54.193
this is getting such attention,

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.029
I think, is because of

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:57.897
the really offensive thing that happened,

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:01.434
which is that disturbed individual

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.869
going into the Covenant School

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:04.671
in Nashville and slaughtering

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:05.571
six innocent people,

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:08.041
including 39 year olds

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.143
at the Covenant School in Nashville.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:13.346
Horrible offensive.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.181
You know, just just a horrific

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.317
mass shooting and

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:20.953
it seems like

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.690
a lot of people outside the legislature

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.792
that lawmakers, Republican lawmakers

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.226
are more concerned

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.529
about a disruption on the floor

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:30.630
than they are about these

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.297
six innocent

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.633
people killed at this Christian school.

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.370
That that's complete nonsense.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.038
That that's the narrative

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.540
that the media is wanted to share.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.809
And that's what these three individuals

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:43.643
are want to share.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.311
There's not one member of that body,

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.746
Republican or Democrat,

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:48.448
that was not devastated by this

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:50.016
horrific, horrendous

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:52.919
action that this lady took down there

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:53.553
in Nashville

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:54.687
when she went in there and murdered

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.357
these six innocent, sweet lives.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.326
When it comes to the legislative process,

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:01.260
these same

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.995
three individuals that are up there

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:05.031
advocating and saying, I'm for gun

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:06.632
or we need in gun violence,

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.400
we need to protect

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.401
our kids were also

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.602
the same three individuals

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.904
that voted against such school

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:14.173
safety perceived bills yesterday.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.376
And just in February,

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:17.510
there was a bill that

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:20.913
Chairman Faison introduced

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:24.684
that would allow more security in co-ops

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:27.687
with private schools and out of the seven

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:28.888
individuals that voted no,

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:29.822
three of them were up

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:30.923
for expulsion yesterday.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:31.324
So it's

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:32.492
very hypocritical

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:33.326
when they want to get up there

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.328
and say we need to stop gun violence

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:37.096
and we need to protect our kids.

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:39.432
Yet they don't vote on legislation

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.067
that would actually end up doing that.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:41.701
And when it comes

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.369
to the legislative process,

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:44.871
we have bill filing deadline

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:46.572
that was back in January

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:47.840
and they didn't submit

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:48.508
any bills

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:49.242
that would end up

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.743
moving through the process.

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.445
And then the state that bills

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.313
that are being voted on now

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:56.349
is just in reaction

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:57.650
to that horrible event

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.852
is nothing close to the truth

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:00.987
because those bills

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:02.522
were filed back in January.

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:03.890
They were planned and prepped

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:05.825
back in October, November and December.

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:06.125
So

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.361
that my heart goes out to the

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:10.029
families and the community.

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:10.830
And this is something

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.498
that should never end up happening,

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:13.599
but it's something that

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.001
every member up there

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:15.601
in the General

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.036
Assembly is working towards

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:17.603
and everybody

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:19.806
trying to make a political statement

00:07:19.806 --> 00:07:20.840
that that's not what's happened.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:23.209
It is so far from the truth. It's absurd.

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:24.076
I'm out of time,

00:07:24.076 --> 00:07:25.545
but I just want to get a yes or no

00:07:25.545 --> 00:07:26.712
on on this.

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:27.980
In the wake of the

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.116
the Parkland School shooting in 2018,

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.718
a lot of states passed red flag laws

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:34.921
that's been encouraged in the

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:37.156
in the national federal legislation

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:39.192
after the Valdez shooting.

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:40.493
But now your governor Bill

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:42.261
Lee Republican suggests

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:44.864
he might be open to a new red flag law.

00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:45.431
Yes or no.

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:46.299
Is that something you'd

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:47.233
be willing to think about?

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:51.971
Can you repeat that last part?

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.439
Would you would you be

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:55.041
would you be willing to support

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:56.142
would you at least be willing

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:58.711
to consider a red flag law for Tennessee?

00:07:58.978 --> 00:07:59.612
To keep guns

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:00.780
out of the hands of individuals

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.515
that have been flagged?

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:04.650
If Governor

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.151
if Governor

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:08.321
Lee brings it to the legislature

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:11.324
I'm not in favor of the term red flag.

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:12.558
Law is so broad

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:14.260
and it covers so many things.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.362
I think that gun

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:18.331
law abiding

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:20.166
citizens should be able to keep guns.

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:21.234
There should be a process

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:22.602
which Tennessee already

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:24.337
has steps for somebody

00:08:24.337 --> 00:08:25.505
to be declared

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:26.973
mentally not stable,

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:28.708
to be able to possess those guns.

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:29.642
That's already on the books.

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:30.977
But everybody wants to overlook that.

00:08:30.977 --> 00:08:33.012
So I would have to look at whatever

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:34.380
particular legislation is.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:35.948
But when it comes to a broad term

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:36.682
red flag law,

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:37.817
now, I'm not in support of that

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:39.585
because I don't know what that entails.

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:40.753
Tennessee state lawmaker

00:08:40.753 --> 00:08:41.220
Bryan Richey,

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.321
thanks for answering your questions

00:08:42.321 --> 00:08:43.155
today. Appreciate it, sir.

